>> title: Tinga de Pollo
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chipotle, tomato, mexican, stovetop, tacos
>> counters: Taquería, One Pot, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: tinga, chicken tinga, tinga poblana, pollo en tinga, tinga de gallina
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, refried-beans
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — a sauce that catches on the bottom of the pan tastes of nothing but scorch afterwards, and it catches fast
>> step.1: poach 25 min, shred
>> step.2: blend smooth
>> step.3: fry the onion 8 min
>> step.4: pour over, reduce 10 min
>> step.5: simmer the chicken in, 10 min

Poach @boneless chicken thighs{2%lb}(900 g; skinless), @white onion{1/2}(halved), @garlic{3%cloves}, @bay leaf{1}, and @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @water{6%cup}(1.4 L) for ~poach{25%min}, then lift the meat out and shred it, keeping a cup of the broth.

Blend @Roma tomatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cored), @chipotles in adobo{3}(plus 1 Tbs of the adobo from the tin), @garlic{2%cloves}, and @dried Mexican oregano{1%tsp} smooth.

Fry @white onion{1%large}(sliced thin) in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a wide #skillet{} for ~fry{8%min}, until it goes limp and gold at the edges.

Pour @&(~2)tomato-chipotle purée{} over @&(~1)softened onion{} and reduce for ~simmer{10%min}, until it darkens and stops tasting raw.

Simmer @&(1)shredded chicken{} in @&(~1)tinga sauce{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp} for ~simmer{10%min}, loosening it with the reserved broth so it stays saucy rather than dry.
